                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="pa-card__body">
                            <div class="pa-alert pa-alert--info">
                                <strong>The problem:</strong> an irregular label set like
                                <em>Orders / Invoices / Delivery sheets / Complaints and missed items</em>
                                looks bad both ways &mdash; <code>--full</code> stretches the short tabs into dead space,
                                and plain auto width leaves the long one huge and the edge ragged.
                                <code>pa-tabs--wrap-labels</code> lets the long title wrap; cap it with
                                <code>maxwr-*</code> to choose the wrap point. The row then keeps every tab as tall
                                as the wrapped one &mdash; no zig-zag &mdash; via the flex row's default
                                <code>align-items: stretch</code>.
                            </div>

                            <h4>Default (auto width, no wrap) &mdash; ragged, long tab dominates</h4>
                            <div class="pa-tabs">
                                <button class="pa-tabs__item pa-tabs__item--active" onclick="switchTab(this, 'wl-auto-1')">Orders</button>
                                <button class="pa-tabs__item" onclick="switchTab(this, 'wl-auto-2')">Invoices</button>
                                <button class="pa-tabs__item" onclick="switchTab(this, 'wl-auto-3')">Delivery sheets</button>
                                <button class="pa-tabs__item" onclick="switchTab(this, 'wl-auto-4')">Complaints and missed items</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="pa-tabs__content">
                                <div class="pa-tabs__panel pa-tabs__panel--active" id="wl-auto-1"><p>Orders content.</p></div>
                                <div class="pa-tabs__panel" id="wl-auto-2"><p>Invoices content.</p></div>
                                <div class="pa-tabs__panel" id="wl-auto-3"><p>Delivery sheets content.</p></div>
                                <div class="pa-tabs__panel" id="wl-auto-4"><p>Complaints content.</p></div>
                            </div>

                            <h4 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">With <code>pa-tabs--wrap-labels</code> + <code>maxwr-15</code> on the long tab &mdash; tidy, level</h4>
                            <div class="pa-tabs pa-tabs--wrap-labels">
                                <button class="pa-tabs__item pa-tabs__item--active" onclick="switchTab(this, 'wl-wrap-1')">Orders</button>
                                <button class="pa-tabs__item" onclick="switchTab(this, 'wl-wrap-2')">Invoices</button>
                                <button class="pa-tabs__item" onclick="switchTab(this, 'wl-wrap-3')">Delivery sheets</button>
                                <button class="pa-tabs__item maxwr-15" onclick="switchTab(this, 'wl-wrap-4')">Complaints and missed items</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="pa-tabs__content">
                                <div class="pa-tabs__panel pa-tabs__panel--active" id="wl-wrap-1"><p>Orders content &mdash; the long tab wraps to two lines; the short tabs stretch to match its height.</p></div>
