                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="pa-card__body">
                    <div class="pa-alert pa-alert--info">
                        A mixed label set like <em>User / Order / Invoice / Packages / Deliveries and returns</em> has a
                        too-narrow first tab and a too-wide last one. Give every tab a <code>minwr-*</code> floor so the
                        short ones stop looking cramped, and cap the long one with <code>maxwr-*</code> (plus
                        <code>pa-tabs--wrap-labels</code> so it wraps) &mdash; the row then stays tidy and level.
                    </div>

                    <h4>Floor every tab at 8rem (<code>minwr-8</code>), cap + wrap the long one (<code>maxwr-15</code>)</h4>
                    <div class="pa-tabs pa-tabs--wrap-labels">
                        <button class="pa-tabs__item minwr-8 pa-tabs__item--active" onclick="switchTab(this, 'rw-tab-1')">User</button>
